WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.968
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Hank Azaria.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.069
Now, we've been talking about
how you've been doing this

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:05.371
a long time.
You do not have --

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:06.873
-A very long time.
-Very long time.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.308
-I'm very tired.
-You've accomplished --

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.609
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.611
It's amazing you have
the energy to even be here.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.912
-It is.
-Based on how long you've been

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.246
doing this.
-Yeah, let's move it along

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:15.248
because --

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.582
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:18.785
-You don't have to audition
anymore, but you did --

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:21.221
and I think this is very helpful
for actors --

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:24.524
you had an ice breaker
in the audition setting.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.525
-[ Laughs ] You've done
your research, sir.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:28.427
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:30.263
Never went well, though,
my "ice breaker."

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.131
-Oh, that's good.
So this is a cautionary tale.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.599
-Well, I was mentioning earlier,
you know,

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:34.833
the absurdity of shooting.

00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:36.869
The whole thing
is kind of crazy.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:40.105
And, so, often you go into
auditions and they'll say --

00:00:40.105 --> 00:00:41.674
you know, there'll be
the producers and the director

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.109
and people, and say,
"Any questions?

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.310
Do you have any questions?"

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.080
Meaning about the script
or the character.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.782
And I would say,
"Yeah, um, so,

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:52.519
I'm supposed to pretend
I'm this guy?"

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.588
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:05.398
And they would look at me and
they'd go, "Yeah. Yeah."

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.768
And I'd say, "And you're
going to point a camera at it,

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.137
but I'm supposed to pretend
I don't notice that?"

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.671
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:15.742
And they would go, "Yeah."

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.245
And I would like at them like
they were insane and go, "Okay."

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.680
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.249
Listen, that did much better
than it ever did in the room.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.650
-Right, right.
Well, that's nice.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.186
We're completing the circle
here.

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:28.020
-They would just --
they would look terrified

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:31.191
and answer earnestly, "Yes,
no, that's right. Yes, yes."

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.393
And then years later,
when I became a producer

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.494
and auditioned a lot of people,
I realized that

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:37.330
actors are often quite crazy.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.332
-Yeah.
-So they might actually --

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.234
-They've heard other versions
of that, probably.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.769
-Oh, you don't know
that somebody is not having

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:46.205
some kind of psychotic break
in front of you.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.708
And need to be reminded that,
yes, the camera is going to be

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.777
there, yeah.
-What about -- this is amazing.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:53.512
34 -- 34th season
of "The Simpsons."

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:54.747
[ Cheer and applause ]

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.016
-Yeah, I mean --
-Yeah.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:59.151
-Well currently, 34 is airing.

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.686
We're currently making 35.

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.755
But who is counting except
for my business manager.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.023
-Right, exactly.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:07.460
And now how -- how much of
your time is now spent --

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.562
and because, again, you do
so many voices on the show --

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.864
-Yeah.
-Is it -- have you become

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:14.967
so efficient that you don't have
to work as many hours doing it?

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.235
Or is it exactly
as much time as --

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:17.770
-[As Moe] I'm going to answer
as Moe, just to --

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.038
-Okay, great, thank you.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.073
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:23.309
-Just 'cause I feel like it.
-Okay.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:26.746
-Yeah, I don't -- I barely work,
like, three minutes.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.781
You know, they show me
the thing, I say the thing,

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.483
and then they send a check,
you know.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.285
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.020
You know.
-There you go. Nice and easy.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.256
-[As Comic Book Guy] Sometimes
Comic Book Guy gets involved.

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:40.760
He says a few things.
Thank you for acknowledging me.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.461
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:45.030
-Now, do you get a little
excited when a new one

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.599
comes up, when they come --
I mean --

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.300
-[Normally] It's rare.
-Yeah, at this point,

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.769
I mean, I feel like they don't
want to overwork you.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.171
There's probably some labor laws
involved of getting --

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.507
-I doubt it.
-Yeah.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:57.143
-No, like, I -- you know,
Jim Brockmire is a guy

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.612
that I did on a TV show.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.213
"Brockmire" is a show I did
for a while.

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:04.550
And he has now found his way
into the show a little bit.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.185
-Oh, they -- he's found his way
into the -- that's wonderful.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:08.588
-Yeah. I just played a --
some kind of a salesman.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.590
I don't remember what --
a car salesman.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.126
And I said, "Ah, let's go with
Jim Brockmire for this one."

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.427
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.429
So, yeah, but they're --
all the voices are, you know,

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.130
relatives or teachers.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.432
-People I grew up with.
-I mean, at what point did

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:22.535
everybody in
your life realize, "Oh, no"?

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.770
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.807
-Oh, I've had --
there was a guy --

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.276
[As Nat ]I did this character on
"Mad About You"

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.278
called Nat the dog Walker.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.546
And he talked like this.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.181
Hey, how you doin' here?

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.682
What's goin' on?

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:39.686
[Normally] And he was based on
a guy I grew up with,

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:42.254
who I ran into
while the show was on.

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:45.892
He said, "Hey!
I saw you on 'Mad About You.'

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.461
How did you think
of that crazy character?"

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.097
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:53.999
I was like, "I don't know.

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:57.102
I just kind of draw on
the people I knew in my life."

00:03:57.102 --> 00:04:00.206
And he did not catch on that --
-Well, there you go.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:03.275
There you go. Well, it's still
a loving tribute either way.

00:04:03.275 --> 00:04:04.377
-Yeah, let's call it that.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.378
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:06.512
-Hey, thanks for being here.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.613
It's always such a pleasure
to see you.

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:09.415
-My pleasure.
-Hank Azaria.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.350
"Hello Tomorrow!" is streaming
on Apple TV+,

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.818
and new episodes
premiering Fridays.

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:14.387
We'll be right back with
Diane Morgan.

